From: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: restore AN7563 TX completion ordering

The AN7563 driver originally recycled entries in its coherent completion
queue immediately before acknowledging them through the QDMA MMIO index.
The ordered MMIO write publishes the preceding coherent-memory updates.

The unified completion path adds an explicit DMA write barrier before
every acknowledgment batch.  Retain that barrier for the newer SoCs,
but avoid the redundant barrier on AN7563 to restore its original TX
completion path.

Signed-off-by: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2972,8 +2972,11 @@ static int airoha_qdma_tx_napi_poll
 	if (done) {
 		int i, len = done >> 7;
 
-		/* Publish empty markers before returning entries to hardware. */
-		dma_wmb();
+		/* Publish empty markers before returning entries to hardware.
+		 * AN7563 relies on the following ordered MMIO acknowledgment.
+		 */
+		if (!airoha_is(qdma->eth, airoha_an7563))
+			dma_wmb();
 
 		for (i = 0; i < len; i++)
 			airoha_qdma_rmw(qdma, REG_IRQ_CLEAR_LEN(id),
-- 
2.51.0
